---
import SiteLayout from "../../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import SupportGuide from "../../../../components/support/SupportGuide.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../../../components/landing/sections/SiteFooter.astro";
import { logicGatesConfig } from "../../../../config/site";
---
<SiteLayout title="Support | Logic Gates" description="Email the Logic Gates developer for questions, feedback, circuit issues or privacy requests." pageType="content">
  <SupportGuide config={logicGatesConfig}>
    <details>
      <summary>Recovery and privacy questions</summary>
      <p>For an accidentally deleted project or folder, check Trash first. Trash has no automatic expiry. Permanent deletion removes its current entry, but earlier recovery saves may retain a copy. Avoid deleting the app if you need help recovering work: the developer has no remote copy of your circuits, and recovery is not guaranteed.</p>
      <p>To move a circuit between devices, use the app's native <code>.logicgates</code> export and import actions where available. An export includes the selected circuit and required definitions, not a complete workspace backup. Check labels and included definitions before sharing. For a file issue, include the format and error message; attach only a small example if needed.</p>
      <p>Deleting the app removes its local data. Exported files, recipients' copies and device backups remain separate; manage those through Files, the provider or your Apple backup settings.</p>
      <p>The same email handles requests about support correspondence. The developer cannot access or erase circuits stored only on your device.</p>
      <p>Logic Gates is intended for learners aged 13 and older. A parent or guardian should send support requests for a child who cannot give valid consent themselves. Avoid including a child's personal information when an anonymous circuit example is enough.</p>
    </details>
  </SupportGuide>
  <SiteFooter links={logicGatesConfig.footerLinks} showBrand={false} showSocials={false} />
</SiteLayout>
